&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Druva&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Druva is the resilience foundation for the AI enterprise, helping organizations secure and recover from connected risk across data, cyber, identity, and AI. The Resilience Cloud is a fully managed, cloud-native SaaS platform that delivers air-gapped and immutable protection across cloud, SaaS, on-premises, endpoint, and edge environments. Powered by Dru MetaGraph, Druva’s graph-powered intelligence layer, the platform connects critical business context so customers can understand risk, respond faster, recover cleanly, and govern data with greater confidence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Trusted by nearly 7,500 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 500, Druva helps safeguard the critical information and systems businesses depend on in an increasingly connected world.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;druva.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and follow us on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/druva/mycompany/&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/druvainc&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/DruvaInc/&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Purpose &amp;amp; Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Druva is seeking a driven and commercially minded Account Executive to lead business development and account growth based in the&lt;strong&gt; UK across EMEA and the Rest of World (ROW)&lt;/strong&gt;. This is a high-impact, new business and expansion role, responsible for increasing adoption of Druva’s Endpoints and Data Security solutions with enterprise, mid-market, and multinational customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with Druva’s regional sales engineers, channel partners, and marketing teams to deliver trusted SaaS solutions that address critical data protection challenges — including GDPR compliance, backup, insider threat protection, and ransomware recovery. Success in this role requires a consultative approach, strong cross-cultural relationship building, and the ability to navigate diverse business practices across multiple countries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Drive sales for Druva’s Endpoints and data protection solutions across assigned accounts in UK, EMEA and ROW.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Consistently achieve or exceed annual revenue targets through a mix of new customer acquisition and existing account growth.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Engage and influence C-level executives, IT leadership, and procurement teams in diverse industry sectors.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Manage complex sales cycles that often involve multiple countries, stakeholders, and decision-making processes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Build and maintain trusted relationships with international channel partners, distributors, and systems integrators.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Deliver compelling, localised solution demonstrations both virtually and onsite.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Maintain awareness of data protection regulations (including GDPR) and regional compliance considerations.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Contribute to a collaborative, customer-first culture within Druva’s international sales team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Travel as required (up to 25%) for customer meetings, events, and partner engagements.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes You a Great Fit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Demonstrated success selling into enterprise and/or commercial organisations across multiple EMEA/UK/ROW markets.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Proven experience in cloud, backup/recovery, cybersecurity, or infrastructure SaaS solutions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Strong track record of exceeding quota in high-growth, competitive markets.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Skilled at managing cross-border sales engagements and adapting to local business cultures.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Experience building strategic relationships with channel partners, distributors, and systems integrators in the region.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with data protection regulations, including GDPR, and their implications for technology adoption.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Ability to influence senior stakeholders and navigate complex buying cycles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Excellent communication, presentation, and negotiation skills across diverse audiences.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Self-starter mentality with a high level of personal drive and accountability.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent professional experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Love Working Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Innovation is how we operate, not a side project. You’ll work in a culture that values bold thinking and continuous improvement, where global teams experiment, iterate, and turn new ideas into products customers can rely on.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re looking for high-ownership work, visible impact, and a culture that values innovation, collaboration, accountability, and growth—where you’ll be trusted to lead and empowered to build—you’ll thrive at Druva.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Druva&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Druva is the resilience foundation for the AI enterprise, helping organizations secure and recover from connected risk across data, cyber, identity, and AI. The Resilience Cloud is a fully managed, cloud-native SaaS platform that delivers air-gapped and immutable protection across cloud, SaaS, on-premises, endpoint, and edge environments. Powered by Dru MetaGraph, Druva’s graph-powered intelligence layer, the platform connects critical business context so customers can understand risk, respond faster, recover cleanly, and govern data with greater confidence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Trusted by nearly 7,500 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 500, Druva helps safeguard the critical information and systems businesses depend on in an increasingly connected world.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;druva.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and follow us on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/druva/mycompany/&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/druvainc&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/DruvaInc/&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Druva delivers data protection and management for the cloud era. Druva Cloud Platform is built on AWS and offered as-a-Service, delivering globally accessible, infinitely scalable and completely autonomous enterprise data resiliency. Customers drive down costs by up to 50 percent by freeing themselves from the burden of unnecessary hardware, capacity planning, and software management. Druva’s patented cloud architecture transforms backup data into an asset, making it more open and accessible so customers can streamline governance, improve cyber resiliency, and gain critical insights to uncover opportunities and expedite decision making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Druva has raised over $350m in venture capital, is trusted by over 4,000 global organizations and protects over 200 PB of data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You&#39;ll work with&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Druva&#39;s Technical Support Team&amp;nbsp; is the focal point for resolution of customer technical issues. We are a worldwide organization of highly skilled engineers that craft and make a positive impact on the customer experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within today&#39;s highly connected and increasingly social world of complex and sophisticated threats, Druva delivers data protection and management for the cloud era. You will be challenged, learn and be energized as you resolve complex technical issues in this ever-evolving landscape. Make an impact by joining the Product Support team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an integral part of the Global Customer Support team, you will provide technical support for Druva products. The Engineer will be responsible for ensuring our customers&#39; success and satisfaction with our products and contributing to their long-term loyalty. You will work closely with the rest of the Druva support team, Engineering, Solutions Delivery, Sales, and Product Management to ensure that Druva is delivering overall superior service and support to our customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities include but are not limited to the following:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be flexible to Work in shift 24 X 7 X 365&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a collaborative team member to resolve issues together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot areas of poor performance and identify effective solutions to resolve issues both in the immediate future and for the longer term.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analysis of exceptions and logs to isolate root cause and help in product’s usability and improve end-user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that knowledge management and data capture processes are adhered to and encourage and help convert technical solutions to Knowledge base articles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approaching complex technical issues with varying perceptions and making use of opportunities to create and implement productivity tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all issues are resolved or escalated to the proper resources to resolve in a timely fashion. Additionally, this individual will manage communications to customers at all levels to maintain positive relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow standard procedures for proper escalation of unresolved issues to the appropriate internal teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow troubleshooting methodology to diagnose, root cause and resolve customer issues, also be able to recreate the issue in-house&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously enhancing knowledge through training and e-learning courses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Quality Assurance and Engineering teams to aid in identifying, reporting, and resolving product defects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with remote support tools and case management systems like Salesforce, JIRA, Zoom &amp;amp; etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meeting Service Level Agreements metric for all customer channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience:&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;3 to 6 years&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree preferably in a technical field and 4+ years’ relevant work experience or equivalent combined training &amp;amp; experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal. Prior Experience in communicating with Enterprise, Service Provider, or SMB customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of backup and recovery concepts&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Types of backups, Replication Etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the following areas:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administrative experience in Operating Systems - Windows, Linux/Unix, Solaris&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge and understanding of cloud infrastructure - AWS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administration &amp;amp; Maintenance Knowledge of&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Microsoft 365&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entra ID&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dynamics 365&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PowerApps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;G Suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Active Directory and API&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with troubleshooting a wide variety of applications using standard tools (etc. Wireshark, tcpdump, procmon, perfmon, OpenSSL)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fundamental knowledge of storage technologies (tape device, SCSI, SAN, iSCSI, NAS etc.) and Networking concepts (routers, firewalls and proxies)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;System Integration - Working knowledge of Identity and Access Management (LDAP, AD, ADFS, Okta, Ping, etc)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to troubleshoot issues involving communication between multiple SaaS and on-premise applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building customer-facing documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with deployment tool (SCCM, JAMF, Quest Kace, Intune etc.) and configuration is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;**If you’re interested in joining the Druva family in a future Sales/Account Executive role in the San Francisco Bay Area, please join our talent community. Submit your resume below, and a recruiter will review and reach out when we have an opportunity arise that matches your skillset &amp;amp; interests. This post is not in reference to a currently open position, but rather in anticipation of future business need.**&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Druva enables cyber, data and operational resilience for every organization with the Data Resiliency Cloud, the industry’s first and only at scale SaaS solution. Customers can radically simplify data protection, streamline data governance, and gain data visibility and insights as they accelerate cloud adoption. Druva pioneered a SaaS-based approach to eliminate complex infrastructure and related management costs, and deliver data resilience via a single platform spanning multiple geographies and clouds. Druva is trusted by thousands of enterprises, including 60 of Fortune 500, to make data more resilient and accelerate their journey to the cloud. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Visit &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;druva.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; and follow us on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/druva/mycompany/&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/druvainc&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/DruvaInc/&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Druva is seeking an MSP Metering &amp;amp; Data Operations Manager to own the operational administration, data integrity, reporting, and forecasting capabilities supporting our global Managed Service Provider business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will serve as the operational owner of the m3ter metering platform and the data flows that underpin MSP consumption, billing, forecasting, and business performance reporting. The successful candidate will combine strong data-analysis skills with hands-on platform administration and business acumen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The primary objective is simple: ensure MSP consumption data is accurate, explainable, actionable, and trusted across the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;m3ter Platform Administration&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- m3ter Platform Administration&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serve as the primary business administrator and subject-matter expert for the m3ter platform supporting Druva&#39;s MSP consumption model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Configure and maintain meters, products, pricing structures, account mappings, and related platform components.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Monitor ingestion and processing of MSP consumption data and identify anomalies, failures, or unexpected results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Coordinate changes to metering logic as Druva introduces new products, SKUs, consumption models, partners, and commercial programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Maintain appropriate documentation, controls, and operating procedures for m3ter administration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Partner with Finance, Deal Desk, Product, Engineering, RevOps, and MSP leadership to ensure metering logic accurately reflects commercial agreements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Data Monitoring &amp;amp; Issue Resolution&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Proactively monitor MSP consumption and metering data for completeness, accuracy, and consistency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Identify discrepancies between source telemetry, m3ter, CRM, billing, and reporting systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Diagnose data issues and determine whether root causes originate from source data, ingestion, mapping, transformation, metering configuration, or reporting logic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Coordinate resolution with Engineering, Finance, RevOps, BI, and other technical teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Establish data-quality checks and exception reporting to identify issues before they affect billing or executive reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Maintain an issue log and drive recurring data problems through root-cause analysis and permanent remediation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Consumption Analytics &amp;amp; Reporting&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Create and maintain dashboards showing MSP consumption and business performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Provide reporting at the global, regional, aggregator, partner, tenant, product, and workload levels as appropriate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Track consumption trends, activations, growth, downsell, churn, product mix, and other key MSP performance indicators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Translate raw consumption data into clear business insights for MSP leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Develop recurring executive reporting that provides a consistent and trusted view of MSP performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Forecasting &amp;amp; Business Intelligence&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Build, maintain, and support MSP forecasting dashboards and underlying data models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Develop consumption-based indicators that improve the accuracy and predictability of ARR forecasts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Track actual consumption and ARR performance against forecast, plan, pacing, and historical trends.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Identify partners, tenants, products, or workloads driving material forecast changes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Provide early-warning indicators for unexpected consumption declines, stalled activations, downsell risk, or unusual growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Support quarter-end forecasting and reconciliation activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cross-Functional Support&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Act as the primary point of contact for questions regarding MSP consumption data and m3ter reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Partner closely with MSP Sales, Finance, RevOps, BI, Engineering, Product, and Deal Desk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Support investigation of partner billing or consumption questions with clear, data-backed explanations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Translate business requirements from MSP leadership into scalable reporting, metering, and analytics solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Reduce manual reporting and reconciliation through automation wherever practical.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key Deliverables&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success in this role will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Reliable operation and administration of the m3ter platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- High confidence in MSP consumption and billing data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Rapid identification and diagnosis of data discrepancies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- A trusted set of MSP consumption and forecast dashboards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Clear reconciliation between consumption, ARR, forecast, and financial reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Automated exception monitoring that identifies issues before they become material.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Reduced manual effort required to produce weekly, monthly, quarterly, and executive MSP reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Qualifications&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- 5+ years of experience in data operations, revenue operations, business intelligence, financial operations, SaaS operations, or a related discipline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Strong experience working with consumption-based or usage-based SaaS business models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Experience administering or supporting metering, billing, subscription-management, or revenue platforms; m3ter experience strongly preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Strong SQL and data-analysis skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Experience building and maintaining dashboards using modern BI/reporting platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Demonstrated ability to troubleshoot complex data flows across multiple systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Strong understanding of SaaS metrics including ARR, consumption, expansion, contraction, churn, and forecasting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Ability to communicate technical data issues clearly to business and executive stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Strong attention to detail combined with the ability to understand the commercial implications behind the data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preferred Experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- MSP, MSSP, cloud services, data protection, or cybersecurity experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Usage-based billing or consumption-based pricing experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Experience integrating CRM, billing, telemetry, and financial systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Familiarity with APIs and modern data pipelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Experience developing automated data-quality and exception-monitoring processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Experience supporting global businesses with multiple currencies, pricing structures, products, and partner models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within the first 6–12 months, this person should become the single trusted operational owner for MSP metering and consumption intelligence. MSP leadership should be able to answer three questions quickly and confidently:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What are our MSPs consuming?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Is the data correct?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What does it tell us about where the business will land?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role should progressively move Druva&#39;s MSP organization from manual reconciliation and retrospective reporting toward automated monitoring, proactive issue detection, and consumption-driven forecasting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;**If you’re interested in joining the Druva family in a future Deal Desk Analyst role in Santa Clara, please join our talent community. Submit your resume below, and a recruiter will review and reach out when we have an opportunity arise that matches your skillset &amp;amp; interests. This post is not in reference to a currently open position, but rather in anticipation of future business need.**&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Druva&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Druva is the resilience foundation for the AI enterprise, helping organizations secure and recover from connected risk across data, cyber, identity, and AI. The Resilience Cloud is a fully managed, cloud-native SaaS platform that delivers air-gapped and immutable protection across cloud, SaaS, on-premises, endpoint, and edge environments. Powered by Dru MetaGraph, Druva’s graph-powered intelligence layer, the platform connects critical business context so customers can understand risk, respond faster, recover cleanly, and govern data with greater confidence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Trusted by nearly 7,500 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 500, Druva helps safeguard the critical information and systems businesses depend on in an increasingly connected world.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;druva.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and follow us on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/druva/mycompany/&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/druvainc&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/DruvaInc/&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;What we would be looking for in the future when a &lt;strong&gt;Deal Desk Analyst&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; position opens up:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Purpose &amp;amp; Impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an energized Deal Desk Analyst to help support our global field sales teams in building pricing proposals and deal structures that provide the optimum balance between the right commercial terms for our customers and the best results for Druva. As a key member of the Deal Desk team, this position will interact with colleagues across Sales, Sales Ops, Finance, Pricing, Order Management, Revenue Ops, and Legal. This individual will help drive standardization and business process improvements that result in increased efficiency and sales velocity as Druva continues to scale and grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with sales teams to structure complex deals, providing guidance that balances profitability with strategic goals and deal velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement by streamlining approval workflows, fixing process gaps, and leveraging AI tools to automate routine tasks and unlock data-driven insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate deal data into actionable intelligence, preparing key reports on renewal metrics, partner incentives, and performance trends to influence leadership strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with Revenue Operations, Legal, Finance, and Product teams to maintain robust compliance and scalable approval processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain documentation to support internal and external processes, ensuring team efficiency and knowledge sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tackle ad-hoc analysis and strategic initiatives to support the scaling needs of the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes You a Great Fit:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–3 years of experience in Deal Desk, Sales Ops, Finance, or Revenue Operations, preferably within the SaaS or enterprise software sector.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Business, Finance, Economics, or a quantitative field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Salesforce (SFDC) and advanced Excel modeling (pivot tables, complex formulas, and scenario analysis).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of SaaS business metrics (ACV, ARR, Churn, Net Retention, ARPU) and their impact on deal profitability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence cross-functional stakeholders (Legal, Sales, Finance, Product) and build productive working relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills, with the ability to prioritize and execute multiple initiatives under tight deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strategic mindset for process improvement and a track record of using AI tools to automate workflows and drive efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success in this role means acting as a high-velocity, strategic engine for sales while safeguarding profitability as Druva scales. You win by partnering with sales teams to architect creative, cross-functionally aligned deal structures that accelerate sales cycles without sacrificing margin. Beyond managing daily deal flow, you drive process transformation by leveraging Salesforce, advanced Excel modeling, and AI automation to eliminate workflow friction and deliver data-driven insights. Ultimately, you serve as a trusted bridge across Sales, Legal, Finance, and RevOps, maintaining flawless compliance while empowering the team to close larger SaaS deals faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Love Working Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Innovation is how we operate, not a side project. You’ll work in a culture that values bold thinking and continuous improvement, where global teams experiment, iterate, and turn new ideas into products customers can rely on.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re looking for high-ownership work, visible impact, and a culture that values innovation, collaboration, accountability, and growth—where you’ll be trusted to lead and empowered to build—you’ll thrive at Druva.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This post is not in reference to a currently open position.&lt;/strong&gt; However, if this position were to open, it would align with the compensation information below.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pay range for this position is expected to be between &lt;strong&gt;$112,000 and $157,333/year;&lt;/strong&gt; however, base pay offered may vary depending on multiple individualized, non-discriminatory factors, including market location, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. The total compensation package for this position may also include other incentive compensation opportunities in the form of discretionary annual bonus or commissions, and equity. Additionally, full-time employees are eligible to participate in our comprehensive benefits program, including health and wellness benefits, 401(k) retirement plan, life and disability insurance coverages, and other benefits the Company may offer from time to time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
