&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Druva&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Druva is the resilience foundation for the AI enterprise, helping organizations secure and recover from connected risk across data, cyber, identity, and AI. The Resilience Cloud is a fully managed, cloud-native SaaS platform that delivers air-gapped and immutable protection across cloud, SaaS, on-premises, endpoint, and edge environments. Powered by Dru MetaGraph, Druva’s graph-powered intelligence layer, the platform connects critical business context so customers can understand risk, respond faster, recover cleanly, and govern data with greater confidence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Trusted by nearly 7,500 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 500, Druva helps safeguard the critical information and systems businesses depend on in an increasingly connected world.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;druva.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and follow us on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/druva/mycompany/&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/druvainc&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/DruvaInc/&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Druva Product Platform&lt;/strong&gt; team builds the shared application platform that every Druva product is built on — the multi-tenant services, APIs, and control-plane capabilities that handle tenant lifecycle and provisioning, identity and access, authorization, configuration, orchestration and job scheduling, metering, and platform-wide observability. When a new workload or product line ships at Druva, it ships on top of what this team owns. That makes the work high-leverage and high-blast-radius in equal measure: the services you own are multi-tenant, always-on, and measured against strict availability and latency objectives, at a scale of thousands of enterprise customers and billions of operations per year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As &lt;strong&gt;Manager, Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;, you will lead a team of 10 to 13 engineers responsible for delivering features and enhancements for scale-out distributed systems and applications on the Druva Product Platform. The role requires involvement across the full product development lifecycle — from product roadmap planning, requirements specification, design, delivery, test, documentation, and release management, through to support and maintenance of what you ship in production. In addition, you will be responsible for talent management activities including mentoring, feedback through regular 1-1s, performance appraisals, and career development for your team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Key Skills:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10-15 years of experience with a consistent track record in development projects involving product development, as both an individual contributor and a team/tech lead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 years managing a team of 5+ engineers, including experience managing, motivating, developing/coaching, and appraising the team assigned to the project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading the development of complex, scale-out, distributed systems based on Service Oriented Architecture/Microservices (preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of modern programming languages such as Go/Python and concepts such as multi-threading, concurrency, data-intensive applications, and NoSQL databases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience building and operating multi-tenant SaaS services — service APIs (REST/gRPC), asynchronous and event-driven workflows, and data stores at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning services in production: availability and latency objectives (SLI/SLO), on-call, incident response, and root cause analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of cloud technologies (AWS / Azure preferred; GCP also relevant) and of containerized deployment (Docker, Kubernetes).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Desirable Skills:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience building products in the areas of Cloud/SaaS services, Storage, Virtualization, or Networking/Security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with platform concerns that cut across products: tenant isolation, authentication and authorization, rate limiting and quotas, schema and API versioning, and safe migration of live tenants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to data protection, backup/recovery, or cyber-resilience domains (RPO/RTO, retention, immutability).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with security and compliance expectations for enterprise SaaS (SOC 2, ISO 27001, GDPR, HIPAA, FedRAMP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping AI-assisted or LLM-backed product capabilities, and the platform work that supports them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start-up development and/or management experience is nice to have.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Role And Responsibilities:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Product Management, UX and architects to come up with high level design for the features, estimates, plan and timelines for the delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a hands-on role that involves understanding the product at a detailed level and contributing to design discussions and code reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define release scope in conjunction with Product Management, and own end-to-end delivery of new features and service releases, often in parallel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the operational health of the services your team runs — availability, latency, and cost objectives — and drive on-call quality, incident response, and follow-through on root cause analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the product teams that build on top of your platform: treat them as customers, set clear API and migration contracts, and manage change without breaking them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help with ongoing escalations as required, and establish lean engineering practices such as CI/CD, TDD, effective code reviews, and automated testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report progress on a timely basis; flag risks early and come up with feasible mitigation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the team structure, and hire and strengthen the team to support the product roadmap and company vision, working closely with Talent Acquisition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach, mentor and provide regular and timely feedback to direct reports; set SMART goals, run performance conversations, and create individual development plans that groom talent for promotion and career growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in customer and sales connect sessions for product feedback, and maintain strong awareness of the market and competing products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Qualification:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.Tech / B.E / M.E / M.Tech (Computer Science) or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Druva&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Druva is the resilience foundation for the AI enterprise, helping organizations secure and recover from connected risk across data, cyber, identity, and AI. The Resilience Cloud is a fully managed, cloud-native SaaS platform that delivers air-gapped and immutable protection across cloud, SaaS, on-premises, endpoint, and edge environments. Powered by Dru MetaGraph, Druva’s graph-powered intelligence layer, the platform connects critical business context so customers can understand risk, respond faster, recover cleanly, and govern data with greater confidence.&lt;br&gt;Trusted by nearly 7,500 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 500, Druva helps safeguard the critical information and systems businesses depend on in an increasingly connected world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;druva.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and follow us on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/druva/mycompany/&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/druvainc&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/DruvaInc/&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be part of a high-impact, fast moving product management team driving our portfolio of products serving partner needs around Data Protection, Cyber Recovery and Response,&amp;nbsp;Disaster Recovery and Governance .&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Purpose &amp;amp; Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Product Manager to help build and scale Druva&#39;s Managed Service Provider (MSP) platform. You will work closely with MSP partners, internal stakeholders,&amp;nbsp;engineering, UX, sales, and customer success to understand partner needs and translate them into product capabilities that simplify service delivery, improve operational efficiency, and&amp;nbsp;accelerate partner growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an excellent opportunity for someone with 3–5 years of Product Management experience who enjoys working directly with customers, solving real business problems, and shipping products that have measurable business impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;● Partner with MSPs, distributors, aggregators and internal teams to understand customer workflows, operational challenges, and emerging market needs.&lt;br&gt;● Gather product requirements through partner interviews and engagements, competitive&amp;nbsp;research, and data analysis.&lt;br&gt;● Prioritize features in collaboration with Engineering and Product leadership.&lt;br&gt;● Write clear Product Requirement Documents (PRDs), user stories, and acceptance&amp;nbsp;criteria.&lt;br&gt;● Drive execution from concept through launch using Agile methodologies.&lt;br&gt;● Collaborate with UX to design intuitive multi-tenant experiences for MSP administrators.&lt;br&gt;● Work with Sales, Customer Success, and Support to identify product improvements and&amp;nbsp;increase partner adoption.&lt;br&gt;● Define success metrics and analyze product telemetry to guide roadmap decisions.&lt;br&gt;● Assist with product launches by creating enablement material, release notes, and&amp;nbsp;customer-facing documentation.&lt;br&gt;● Represent the voice of MSP customers during planning and sprint reviews.&lt;br&gt;● Stay current on trends in managed services, SaaS, cloud infrastructure, backup, cyber&amp;nbsp;resilience, and channel ecosystems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What makes you a great fit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;● 3–5 years of Product Management experience building B2B SaaS products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Managed Service Providers (MSPs), Distributors, Value Added Resellers (VARs), or other channel partners preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with building products for marketplaces, integrations, or multi-tenant&amp;nbsp;SaaS platforms preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;● Bachelor&#39;s degree in Engineering, Computer Science, or related field.&lt;br&gt;● Experience writing detailed product requirements and working closely with engineering teams.&lt;br&gt;● Strong understanding of Agile development methodologies.&lt;br&gt;● Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills.&lt;br&gt;● Strong communication and stakeholder management skills.&lt;br&gt;● Passion for understanding customer problems and turning them into simple product experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like in the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;● Help solve key challenges around MSP scalability, workflow simplification, integrations, and partner experience.&lt;br&gt;● Become the trusted owner of a product area, delivering customer-focused solutions that&amp;nbsp;drive measurable business outcomes.&lt;br&gt;● Build strong partnerships across Engineering, Design, Sales, Customer Success, and&amp;nbsp;partners to execute effectively.&lt;br&gt;● Use customer feedback, market insights, and product data to prioritize initiatives that&amp;nbsp;improve adoption, retention, and revenue.&lt;br&gt;● Deliver roadmap commitments with high quality, proactively managing trade-offs, risks,&amp;nbsp;and dependencies.&lt;br&gt;● Demonstrable impact on product KPIs (e.g., adoption, engagement, retention, revenue,&amp;nbsp;partner satisfaction).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Love Working Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Innovation is how we operate, not a side project. You’ll work in a culture that values bold thinking and continuous improvement, where global teams experiment, iterate, and turn new&amp;nbsp;ideas into products customers can rely on.&amp;nbsp;If you’re looking for high-ownership work, visible impact, and a culture that values innovation,&amp;nbsp;collaboration, accountability, and growth—where you’ll be trusted to lead and empowered to&amp;nbsp;build—you’ll thrive at Druva.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Druva&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Druva is the resilience foundation for the AI enterprise, helping organizations secure and recover from connected risk across data, cyber, identity, and AI. The Resilience Cloud is a fully managed, cloud-native SaaS platform that delivers air-gapped and immutable protection across cloud, SaaS, on-premises, endpoint, and edge environments. Powered by Dru MetaGraph, Druva’s graph-powered intelligence layer, the platform connects critical business context so customers can understand risk, respond faster, recover cleanly, and govern data with greater confidence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Trusted by nearly 7,500 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 500, Druva helps safeguard the critical information and systems businesses depend on in an increasingly connected world.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;druva.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and follow us on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/druva/mycompany/&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/druvainc&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/DruvaInc/&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Office of the CEO sits at the center of Druva&#39;s strategic and operational priorities, partnering closely with the CEO and executive team to drive company-wide initiatives from concept to execution. The team operates as a small, high-trust group that moves fluidly across strategy, operations, and special projects, often stepping in wherever the business needs the most leverage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Purpose &amp;amp; Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Project Lead, Strategic Planning and Operations, will own a critical portion of the rhythm of the business across three major categories: Business Planning, Strategic Operations, and Strategy. This role operates with significant autonomy, sets the approach for high-stakes cross-functional initiatives, and is trusted to represent the Office of the CEO directly with senior stakeholders. This is a high-impact, high-visibility role reporting into the Office of the CEO, with the latitude to shape how the company plans, decides, and executes at the highest level.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Insights, Decision Support and Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently drive research and analysis on complex business trends, competitive dynamics, and market conditions to inform CEO- and board-level decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize ambiguous or incomplete data into clear strategic recommendations, proactively identifying risks and opportunities before they&#39;re raised.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted thought partner to senior leaders, shaping strategic narratives rather than simply supporting them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Project Management and Cross-Functional Coordination:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end delivery of the company&#39;s highest-priority, most complex initiatives, often spanning multiple departments, external stakeholders, and ambiguous scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set project strategy, timelines, and success metrics with minimal oversight; anticipate roadblocks and course-correct proactively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a primary liaison across departments and with executive stakeholders, resolving cross-functional conflicts and driving alignment at the leadership level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver polished, executive-ready updates directly to the CEO and executive staff, exercising judgment on what to escalate versus own independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Corporate Planning and Alignment: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the design and execution of the corporate operating rhythm (Company All Hands, Quarterly Business Reviews, E-Staff Meetings), including agenda strategy, executive content development, and follow-through on action items.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improve how the company plans and communicates at the executive level, introducing new frameworks or processes as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes You a Great Fit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Business Administration, Management, Engineering, or a related field; MBA a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5+ years of professional experience, ideally within top-tier consulting, corporate strategy, or a high-growth SaaS environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established track record of partnering directly with, advising, and influencing senior/executive leadership on high-stakes decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of business operations, strategy development, and SaaS business models, with the judgment to apply that understanding independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to operate with a high degree of autonomy and ambiguity — setting direction, not just executing against it — while maintaining exceptional attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written, verbal, and interpersonal skills; high emotional intelligence and executive presence, with the adaptability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-stakes environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making capabilities, including the ability to structure ambiguous problems from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to maintain strict confidentiality and navigate highly sensitive information with integrity and discretion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in Google Workspace, Microsoft Office Suite, and standard modern business tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of AI/LLM-based tools (e.g., Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini, or similar) and how to apply them to accelerate research, synthesis, drafting, and data analysis; comfort evaluating where AI tools can improve the speed and quality of strategic work, and judgment about their limitations in high-stakes or confidential contexts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the first six months, success will be ramping quickly to understand the Druva business and adding value through strategic analysis and project leadership. Business partners will look to you as a trusted team member. Longer term, success means the corporate operating rhythm runs more effectively because of the frameworks and improvements you&#39;ve introduced, and that you&#39;re recognized as a multiplier for the Office of the CEO&#39;s impact across the company.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Love Working Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Innovation is how we operate, not a side project. You’ll work in a culture that values bold thinking and continuous improvement, where global teams experiment, iterate, and turn new ideas into products customers can rely on.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re looking for high-ownership work, visible impact, and a culture that values innovation, collaboration, accountability, and growth—where you’ll be trusted to lead and empowered to build—you’ll thrive at Druva.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pay range for this position is expected to be between&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;$112,000 and $157,333/year;&lt;/strong&gt; however, base pay offered may vary depending on multiple individualized, non-discriminatory factors, including market location, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. The total compensation package for this position may also include other incentive compensation opportunities in the form of discretionary annual bonus or commissions, and equity. Additionally, full-time employees are eligible to participate in our comprehensive benefits program, including health and wellness benefits, 401(k) retirement plan, life and disability insurance coverages, and other benefits the Company may offer from time to time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
